99,"d":1841},{"n":"Farmacia Cristoforo Colombo","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":44.346176,"lo":9.227713,"d":1842},{"n":"Hannibal's Bridge","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.3469,"lo":9.2271,"d":1870,"ds":"Hannibal's Bridge (Italian: Ponte Annibale) at Rapallo, Italy is one of the oldest structures in the city. This bridge was possibly used by Carthaginian commander Hannibal during his campaign against Rome in the Second Punic War, where he unloaded supplies on the Tigullia coast (region from Portofino to Anzo di Framura). The bridge could also be connected to the Battle of Trebbia (218 BC).","wpu":"Hannibal's Bridge","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Hannibal_Bridge%2C_Rapallo%2C_2026.png/960px-Hannibal_Bridge%2C_Rapallo%2C_2026.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Cervara Abbey","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.3133,"lo":9.2134,"d":2304,"ds":"Cervara Abbey (Italian: Abbazia della Cervara or Abbazia di San Gerolamo al Monte di Portofino) is a former abbey in Santa Margherita Ligure, Liguria region, northern Italy. It is on the coastal road to Portofino. The abbey complex is a designated National Monument of Italy.","wpu":"Cervara Abbey","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Cervara01.jpg/960px-Cervara01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Paraggi","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.311111,"lo":9.208889,"d":2557,"ds":"Paraggi is a bay between Santa Margherita Ligure and Portofino. Paraggi beach is a tourist attraction known for its crystal clear blue water. Paraggi beach is a fishing location and a popular attraction for tourists because it is the only sandy beach near Portofino.","wpu":"Paraggi","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Paraggi_Beach_Near_Portofino_Italy_2019.jpg/960px-Paraggi_Beach_Near_Portofino_Italy_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Belmond Hotel Splendido","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.303304,"lo":9.20923,"d":3420,"ds":"The Belmond Hotel Splendido is a hotel in Portofino, Italy. The site was formerly home to a Benedictine monastery which was ransacked so many times by Saracen pirates that the monks abandoned it in the 16th century. The four-storey high building subsequently fell into disrepair.","wpu":"Belmond Hotel Splendido","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Belmond_Hotel_Splendido%2C_Portofino%2C_Italy.jpg/960px-Belmond_Hotel_Splendido%2C_Portofino%2C_Italy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"San Fruttuoso Abbey","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.3164,"lo":9.1752,"d":3521,"ds":"San Fruttuoso Abbey (Italian: Abbazia di San Fruttuoso) is a Romanesque religious building located in a secluded bay in the Italian Riviera near Genoa, between Camogli and Portofino, The abbey used to be under the patronage of the Genoese aristocratic Doria family, who protected it with a watchtower built by the architect Giovanni Ponzello in 1562.","wpu":"San Fruttuoso Abbey","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Abbey_of_San_Fruttuoso_Camogli_Liguria.jpg/960px-Abbey_of_San_Fruttuoso_Camogli_Liguria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Castello Brown","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.302078,"lo":9.214306,"d":3554,"ds":"Castello Brown is a historic house museum located above the harbour of Portofino, in northern Italy. The site has been used for military defence since Roman times. As a Genoese coastal fort, it was once called the Castello di San Giorgio.","wpu":"Castello Brown","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Castello_Brown_Portofino_Liguria.jpg/960px-Castello_Brown_Portofino_Liguria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"San Giorgio, Portofino","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.301456,"lo":9.211564,"d":3618,"ds":"San Giorgio is a Roman Catholic church located in Portofino, Italy.","wpu":"San Giorgio, Portofino","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Portofino-chiesa_san_Giorgio_%282012%29.JPG/960px-Portofino-chiesa_san_Giorgio_%282012%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Christ of the Abyss","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.314038,"lo":9.174979,"d":3687,"ds":"Christ of the Abyss (Italian: Il Cristo degli Abissi) is a submerged bronze statue of Jesus Christ by Guido Galletti, the original cast of which is located in the Mediterranean Sea, off San Fruttuoso, between Camogli and Portofino on the Italian Riviera. Various other casts of the statue are located in other places worldwide, in underwater locations, churches and museums.","wpu":"Christ of the Abyss","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/96/Cristo_degli_abissi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Portofino Lighthouse","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.298682,"lo":9.218398,"d":3960,"ds":"Portofino Lighthouse (Italian: Faro di Portofino) is an active lighthouse located in Portofino, Metropolitan City of Genoa, Liguria, northern Italy, on the western extremity of the peninsula in the Gulf of Tigullio.","wpu":"Portofino Lighthouse","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/LightPortofino.jpg/960px-LightPortofino.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Sem Benelli Castle","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.333753,"lo":9.274017,"d":4932,"ds":"The Sem Benelli Castle (Italian: Castello Sem Benelli) is a historic villa located in Zoagli, Italy.","wpu":"Sem Benelli Castle","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Zoagli%2C_Liguria%2C_Italia_-_Flickr_-_pom%27..jpg/960px-Zoagli%2C_Liguria%2C_Italia_-_Flickr_-_pom%27..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Sanctuary of Our Lady of Montallegro","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.37,"lo":9.255556,"d":5293,"ds":"The basilica sanctuary of Our Lady of Montallegro is a place of Catholic worship located in the hamlet of Montallegro in the municipality of Rapallo, in the metropolitan city of Genoa. The building is located on a hill about 612 m above sea level.","wpu":"Sanctuary of Our Lady of Montallegro","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Santuario_di_Nostra_Signora_di_Montallegro_%28Montallegro%2C_Rapallo%29_-_facciata_2022-06-10.jpg/960px-Santuario_di_Nostra_Signora_di_Montallegro_%28Montallegro%2C_Rapallo%29_-_facciata_2022-06-10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Camogli Molo Esterno Lighthouse","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.351783,"lo":9.149192,"d":5371,"ds":"Camogli Molo Esterno Lighthouse (Italian: Faro di Camogli Molo Esterno) is an active lighthouse located at the end of the external breakwater of the harbour of Camogli, Liguria on the Ligurian Sea.","wpu":"Camogli Molo Esterno Lighthouse","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/Faro_Camogli_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Chiavari Castle","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.318889,"lo":9.326389,"d":9252,"ds":"Chiavari Castle (Castello di Chiavari) is an ancient fortification in Chiavari, Province of Genoa, in Italy.","wpu":"Chiavari Castle","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fc/Chiavari_castle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Diocese of Chiavari","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":44.3167,"lo":9.3333,"d":9838,"ds":"The Diocese of Chiavari (Latin: Dioecesis Clavarensis) is a Latin diocese of the Catholic Church in Liguria, northern Italy. It was created on 3 December 1892 by Pope Leo XIII in the Bull Romani Pontifices. It is a suffragan of the Archdiocese of Genoa.","wpu":"Diocese of Chiavari","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Chiavari%2C_Cattedrale_di_Nostra_Signora_dell%27Orto_01.JPG/960px-Chiavari%2C_Cattedrale_di_Nostra_Signora_dell%27Orto_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Santa Margherita Ligure (Italian: [ˈsanta marɡeˈriːta ˈliːɡure]; Ligurian: Santa Margàita [ˈsaŋta maɾˈɡajta]) is a comune (municipality) in the Metropolitan City of Genoa in the Italian region of Liguria, located about 35 kilometres (22 mi) southeast of Genoa, in the area traditionally known as Tigullio. It has a port, used for both tourism and fishing activities. Part of comune territory is included in the Regional Natural Park of Portofino.","wpu":"Santa Margherita Ligure","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Santa_Margherita_Ligure%2C_Italy.jpg/960px-Santa_Margherita_Ligure%2C_Italy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}